When implementing changes:

- First analyze related files.
- Explain the plan briefly.
- Then implement changes carefully.
- Avoid breaking existing flows.

Engineering workflow:

- Never modify many unrelated files at once.
- Prefer incremental safe changes.
- Before coding, identify affected screens, services, hooks and navigation flows.
- Explain risks before implementing.
- Preserve existing business logic unless explicitly asked to change it.
- Avoid introducing new libraries unless necessary.
- Respect Expo compatibility.
- Keep React Navigation patterns consistent.
- Reuse existing Firebase abstractions.
- Avoid duplicating Firestore queries.
- Maintain backward compatibility for existing users.
- Be careful with profile completion logic and onboarding flow.
- Always analyze Android and iOS differences before changing Firebase code.

Code style:

- Prefer readable code over clever code.
- Keep components modular.
- Avoid giant components.
- Use hooks responsibly.
- Avoid unnecessary state duplication.
- Prefer typed interfaces.
- Keep async flows predictable.
- Avoid navigation reset hacks unless necessary.

When debugging:

- First explain probable root cause.
- Then explain affected files.
- Then propose minimal fix.
- Then implement carefully.
